<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The hemogen rush: on the pilot while the armor's toggle is on (AbilityDefs/HemogenRush.xml).

    Buff:
    - Consciousness +0.2, go-juice's. Not its painFactor: the pilot's trait already takes all
      pain away (TraitDefs/WarcasketTrait_Hemophage.xml), and the rush ends with the armor off.
    - MeleeDamageFactor 1.5, juggernaut serum's. On the sanguophage's MeleeDamage_Strong
      gene that is 2.25, as the serum is.
    - Move speed 1.5 in all, under rage speed's 1.75, in two parts. BloodPumping +1 is the
      injectors at work, 200% on the Health tab. Moving takes 0.2 of blood pumping's gain,
      where Consciousness stops reading it at 1 (their capacity workers; 1.6 and 1.7), so it
      comes to Moving 1.2, which is move speed 1.2 and at most 7 points of melee dodge. The
      one stat that reads it directly is the rest rate, and a rush ends with sleep.
      MoveSpeed 1.25 is the rest. Both multiply, so the gain scales with the pilot's own
      speed: a sanguophage's 4.8 cells a second becomes 7.2, about an unarmored baseliner's
      on go-juice. The offset adds to whatever else raises the pilot's blood pumping, a
      bionic heart for one, and a destroyed heart takes none, since the game adds offsets
      only to a capacity above 0.
    Melee cooldown is left alone: with the damage factor it would about double melee output.

    Drain: hemogenPerSecond 0.02 is 2 hemogen a second on the scale the game shows, and one
    hemogen pack buys 10 seconds. hemogenStartCost 0.05 is 5 hemogen spent as the rush
    starts, 2.5 seconds of the drain and about one melee swing, so switching the rush on for
    each blow costs more than leaving it running. A full 100 lasts 47.5 seconds.
    hemogenReserve 0 runs the pilot dry, which starts hemogen craving as any other way of
    reaching zero does. The start cost never takes the pilot below the reserve: the toggle
    is refused unless more than the cost is spare.

    The toggle settles on the next tick: the rush shows at the click, the start cost is paid
    on the rush's first tick and a stop is carried out on the tick after it is asked for.
    The glow answers the click both ways, on with the rush and off with the stop. Clicks
    made in a pause therefore net out to the last one, and switching a rush off and on again
    without letting the game run costs nothing (HediffComp_HemogenRush).

    Ends when toggled off, at the reserve, when the pilot is downed, asleep, no longer
    hemogenic, out of the armor or, for a player's pilot, out of the player's control (a mental
    break, leaving the map), all in HediffComp_HemogenRush, on death and at the start of a
    deathrest. Drafting and undrafting leave it running.

    Glow: every worn piece of the set draws its glow sprite while the pilot has this hediff
    and has not switched it off (the pieces' renderNodeProperties). forceRenderTreeRecache
    makes the game rebuild the pilot's graphics when it is added or removed. glowPulse is a
    heartbeat, two dips a beat from full strength, never below 0.25 so the glow never goes
    out, one beat a second at normal speed. It rests at full strength, the strength
    portraits and the zoomed-out pawn cache bake, and the strength the glow holds with
    glowPulses off.

    Sparks: the pilot gives off EffecterDefs/HemogenRush.xml for as long as the hediff
    is on them, through the game's own HediffCompProperties_Effecter.

    The mod settings override hemogenStartCost, hemogenPerSecond, hemogenReserve, glowPulses
    and the two statFactors (Source/1.6/Settings/Settings_Rush.cs). Their move speed is the
    1.5 in all, written as the MoveSpeed factor that reaches it beside the blood pumping.

    defaultLabelColor is the drug highs'.
  -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>HPWC_HemogenRush</defName>
    <label>hemogen rush</label>
    <description>This person's warcasket is pumping hemogen through their body, allowing them to move faster and hit harder. Their hemogen will run down quickly while this lasts.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <defaultLabelColor>(1, 0, 0.5)</defaultLabelColor>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <removeOnDeathrestStart>true</removeOnDeathrestStart>
    <forceRenderTreeRecache>true</forceRenderTreeRecache>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HemophageWarcasket.HediffCompProperties_HemogenRush">
        <hemogenStartCost>0.05</hemogenStartCost>
        <hemogenPerSecond>0.02</hemogenPerSecond>
        <hemogenReserve>0</hemogenReserve>
        <armor>HPWC_Warcasket_Hemophage</armor>
        <glowPulses>true</glowPulses>
        <glowPulseTicks>60</glowPulseTicks>
        <glowPulse>
          <points>
            <li>(0, 1)</li>
            <li>(0.1, 0.25)</li>
            <li>(0.24, 0.85)</li>
            <li>(0.36, 0.4)</li>
            <li>(0.6, 1)</li>
            <li>(1, 1)</li>
          </points>
        </glowPulse>
      </li>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_Effecter">
        <stateEffecter>HPWC_HemogenRush</stateEffecter>
      </li>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_DisappearsOnDeath" />
    </comps>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>0.2</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>BloodPumping</capacity>
            <offset>1</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
        <statFactors>
          <MoveSpeed>1.25</MoveSpeed>
          <MeleeDamageFactor>1.5</MeleeDamageFactor>
        </statFactors>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>
</Defs>
